			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">As some of you may recall, I was recently investigating what the deal is with Nabisco Pinwheels and Twirls.  For those of you who don't know, these are the round cookies, with a cookie bottom, marshmellow on top, a hole in the center, and covered in a chocolate coating.
<br />

<br />
My concern (and curiousity) had to do with both Pinwheels and Twirls looking identical, but tasting different.  I personally adore Pinwheels, but only moderately like Twirls.  Lately I have only been able to find Twirls.  Is one going to replace the other?  Are they just two separate but strangely similar cookie lines?  I wrote Nabisco to find out.
<br />

<br />
Nabisco reported back to me.  Although the reason behind the issue makes perfect sense, it hadn't occurred to me until they reported back.  Here is what they had to say:
<br />

<br />
</span><table width="90%" cellspacing="1" cellpadding="3" border="0" align="center"><tr> 	  <td><span class="genmed"><b>Nabisco wrote:</b></span></td>	</tr>	<tr>	  <td class="quote">Thank you for contacting us concerning the availability of Marshmallow
<br />
Pinwheel Cakes. We certainly appreciate your interest in this product. 
<br />

<br />
During the summer months, we suspend production of items such as this one
<br />
because of the low melting point and possible discoloration of the pure
<br />
chocolate coating.  A similar product, Marshmallow Twirls, is available
<br />
throughout the year.  It is made with a cocoa coating that tolerates
<br />
temperature changes better than pure chocolate. 
<br />

<br />
In early fall, Marshmallow Pinwheel Cakes will reappear on your grocer's
<br />
shelf!  
<br />

<br />
Thanks again for your interest and for being such a loyal Marshmallow
<br />
Pinwheel Cakes consumer!</td>	</tr></table><span class="postbody">
<br />

<br />
So there it is.  Now I know why Twirls do not taste as good.  And now I finally have a reason to look foward to Winter.<br />_________________<br />[65 Arch Convoker] <a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=132081" target="_blank" class="postlink">Skotty</a> (Human)
<br />
