		<td class="row2" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=60759&amp;sid=71f38f059beddf46f083876f1d07f8ba#60759"><img src="templates/subSilver/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Sat Jun 12, 2004 6:52 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: Re: Pinwheels vs Twirls</span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=60759&amp;sid=71f38f059beddf46f083876f1d07f8ba"><img src="templates/subSilver/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody"></span><table width="90%" cellspacing="1" cellpadding="3" border="0" align="center"><tr> 	  <td><span class="genmed"><b>Skotty wrote:</b></span></td>	</tr>	<tr>	  <td class="quote">As some of you may recall, I was recently investigating what the deal is with Nabisco Pinwheels and Twirls.  For those of you who don't know, these are the round cookies, with a cookie bottom, marshmellow on top, a hole in the center, and covered in a chocolate coating.
<br />

<br />
My concern (and curiousity) had to do with both Pinwheels and Twirls looking identical, but tasting different.  I personally adore Pinwheels, but only moderately like Twirls.  Lately I have only been able to find Twirls.  Is one going to replace the other?  Are they just two separate but strangely similar cookie lines?  I wrote Nabisco to find out.
<br />

<br />
Nabisco reported back to me.  Although the reason behind the issue makes perfect sense, it hadn't occurred to me until they reported back.  Here is what they had to say:
<br />

<br />
</span><table width="90%" cellspacing="1" cellpadding="3" border="0" align="center"><tr> 	  <td><span class="genmed"><b>Nabisco wrote:</b></span></td>	</tr>	<tr>	  <td class="quote">Thank you for contacting us concerning the availability of Marshmallow
<br />
Pinwheel Cakes. We certainly appreciate your interest in this product. 
<br />

<br />
During the summer months, we suspend production of items such as this one
<br />
because of the low melting point and possible discoloration of the pure
<br />
chocolate coating.  A similar product, Marshmallow Twirls, is available
<br />
throughout the year.  It is made with a cocoa coating that tolerates
<br />
temperature changes better than pure chocolate. 
<br />

<br />
In early fall, Marshmallow Pinwheel Cakes will reappear on your grocer's
<br />
shelf!  
<br />

<br />
Thanks again for your interest and for being such a loyal Marshmallow
<br />
Pinwheel Cakes consumer!</td>	</tr></table><span class="postbody">
<br />

<br />
So there it is.  Now I know why Twirls do not taste as good.  And now I finally have a reason to look foward to Winter.</td>	</tr></table><span class="postbody">
<br />

<br />
I stop by to check in on things and see this.  Dear Lord, why did I stay away so long!  Skotty, you sir, R O C K!   <img src="images/smiles/icon_exclaim.gif" alt="icon_exclaim.gif" border="0" />
<br />

<br />
P.S.  I'm playing a 'Healer' in City of Heroes.  I hereby formally apologize to any clerics I harassed in EQ.
<br />

<br />
Fluxus</span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
			</tr>
